# Trivy misconfiguration scan: accepted findings.
# Every entry needs a reason. Review them when the modules change.
# Scan: trivy config --ignorefile .trivyignore .

# GCP-0066 (LOW) Storage bucket encryption does not use a customer-managed key.
# modules/gcs-migration-staging: CMEK is optional on purpose. Set
# staging_bucket_kms_key_name (Scenario 2) to use a Cloud KMS key; the default
# is Google-managed encryption, which is acceptable for a short-lived staging
# bucket that also has public access prevention, uniform bucket-level access,
# versioning and a delete lifecycle.
GCP-0066
